      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Please do not administer any insulin, especially long-acting insulin like Lantus, when you are experiencing hypoglycemia. Taking insulin when your blood sugar is low will likely make the low much worse and could be life-threatening. Your immediate priority must be treating the low with fast-acting sugar; once your blood sugar is stable and back into a safe range, you can consult your healthcare provider about adjusting your insulin dosing. If you are very concerned about a future high, always contact your diabetes care team before making any insulin changes.",
